      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (about 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day** split into doses, such as 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg** PO two or three times daily, which is a more typical starting dose\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and add a note on why, and I'll enter it that way."
      }
